{"name":"Early Crocus","hex":"#eae7e7","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"early","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["At a time in advance of the usual or expected event.","Arriving a time before expected; sooner than on time."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A shift (scheduled work period) that takes place early in the day."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/early"},{"term":"crocus","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A perennial flowering plant (of the genus Crocus in the Iridaceae family). Saffron is obtained from the stamens of Crocus sativus.","Any of various similar flowering plants, such as autumn crocus and prairie crocus."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A fraudulent doctor; a quack."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/crocus"}],"entries":[{"title":"Crocus tommasinianus","blocks":[{"text":"Crocus tommasinianus, the woodland crocus, early crocus, or Tommasini's crocus, is a species of flowering plant in the family Iridaceae. It is named after the botanist Muzio G. Spirito de Tommasini (1794–1879). It is native to Bulgaria, Hungary, Albania, and the former Yugoslavia. It is often referred to as the early or snow crocus, but these terms are shared with several other species, although C. tommasinianus is amongst the first to bloom. Multiple plants are often called tommies in the horticultural trade."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/ba/Crocus_tommasinianus_%28Xytram%29.jpg/330px-Crocus_tommasinianus_%28Xytram%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Crocus_tommasinianus"},{"title":"Crocus","blocks":[{"text":"Crocus is a genus of seasonal flowering plants in the family Iridaceae comprising about 100 species of perennials growing from corms."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/2c/860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2.jpg/330px-860808-Saffronfarm-01-IMG_7707-2